---
// SOW-119 / sow-243: the Codeable expert invite landing. Since 2026-09-11 this page is CAMPAIGN DATA and copy
// only; the chrome (nav, hero grid, sticky claim card, coupon chip, Turnstile-gated CTA and its script, FAQ
// accordion, footer, styles) lives once in src/components/invite/InviteLander.astro. It used to be a full copy
// of that markup here, and two more copies at /member-invite/ and /curator-invite/.
//
// THIS INVITE CONFERS `member`, NOT `creator` (owner ruling 2026-08-24: the coupons "should only offer
// membership rather than creator"). house/coupons.yml names `tier: member` on CODEABLEYEAR, and that tier is
// stamped into the redemption record, so this page and the grant agree only if BOTH say member. The constants
// are named for what they are; `const creator = tierDisplay('member')` would be a false name.
//
// THE BENEFIT LIST IS RENDERED FROM house/membership-tiers.yml AND IS NOT WRITTEN HERE. A hand-written array
// once carried Creator claims that no string check could see, because a sentence promising publishing never
// names a tier or a price. If a claim is not a bullet in that file, it cannot reach this page.
//
// NO BENEFIT LIST IN THE FAQ, NO REVENUE COPY (banned-patterns.md #2). Every answer that sold a Creator
// benefit is gone rather than reworded. The tier name and the price come from tierDisplay(), so no answer can
// quote a stale figure. Any sentence about what a tier is belongs HERE, in this page's data, never in the
// shared template: a template that interpolated a label but kept "the network's top tier" would advertise the
// wrong tier at the right price, which is the trap sow-243 names.
//
// THE CAMPAIGN. A shared link carries a plain visible ?coupon=CODEABLEYEAR, which prefills the coupon field
// (QA 2026-07-18: no secret token links); with no parameter the field is hand-editable. The parity test reads
// this line to check that the campaign's tier and this page's tier agree.
import InviteLander from '../../components/invite/InviteLander.astro';
import { BILLING_PERIOD } from '../../lib/membership';
import { tierDisplay, tierLabel, TIER } from '../../lib/tiers'; // sow-316: tierLabel NAMES a tier; tierDisplay binds this page's product

const memberTier = tierDisplay('member');
const TIER_LABEL = memberTier?.label ?? 'Network Member';
const TIER_PRICE_LABEL = `$${memberTier?.priceAnnual ?? 50}`;
const memberBenefits = memberTier?.benefits ?? [];

const faqs = [
  ['What does this invite give me?', `A full year at the ${TIER_LABEL} tier, with everything listed above, at no cost. It is a normal membership for the year, not a limited preview.`],
  ['Do I need a card to claim it?', 'No. No card is collected at any point during the free year, and nothing bills automatically.'],
  ['What happens when the free year ends?', `Nothing happens on its own. ${TIER_LABEL} is ${TIER_PRICE_LABEL} per ${BILLING_PERIOD} if you decide to continue, and you will not be charged unless you choose to.`],
  ['How do I claim it?', 'Sign in with GitHub from this page. Your coupon is already applied, so there is nothing to enter or remember.'],
  ['Can I pass this on to someone else?', 'It is meant for you, but the link works for whoever opens it first, so treat it as personal rather than forwardable.'],
  ['What is the GBTI Network?', `A professional publishing network for developers. Members read and discuss the work published across it and take part in a private community. Publishing your own articles, projects and prompts is the ${tierLabel(TIER.creator)} tier.`],
  // ASKED AND ANSWERED PLAINLY, because the audience makes it the obvious question. Codeable experts are
  // working professionals, and the page they were sent used to promise publishing.
  ['Can I publish my own work with this invite?', `Not on this invite. Publishing articles, projects and prompts is the ${tierLabel(TIER.creator)} tier, and this covers a year at ${TIER_LABEL}: reading members-only work, commenting anywhere on the network, and full Discord access. You can move up whenever you want to publish.`],
  ['Is all content public or private?', 'Both. Some work is published openly, and some is network-only. For network-only work, a stub with a short description appears on the public website, while the full content is readable by members inside the login-gated browser extension.'],
  ['Are comments on public-facing content also public?', 'By default, they are not, and can only be read inside the extension by other members. There is, however, the option to make a comment fully public.'],
  ['What does GBTI stand for?', 'God Bless The Internet; a phrase that expresses appreciation and goodwill toward the continued growth and enrichment of the internet.'],
  // The founding story is a FACT about GBTI and stays true whatever tier the invite confers. The sentence
  // about Codeable is the one thing on this page that is genuinely audience-specific and is sourced.
  ['Why is my first year free?', `The GBTI Network was founded by members of the Codeable network seeking a place to discuss the nuances of project development. The expertise at Codeable is well known and respected, and we are happy to be an answer to any interest in community that Codeable experts might have. As a Codeable expert your first year at the ${TIER_LABEL} tier is on us.`],
] as const;
---

<InviteLander
  title="Codeable experts: your first year on us"
  description="A private invitation for Codeable experts: a full year of Network Member access, first year free with your coupon."
  tierLabel={TIER_LABEL}
  tierPriceLabel={TIER_PRICE_LABEL}
  benefits={memberBenefits}
  benefitsHeading={`What ${TIER_LABEL} gives you`}
  benefitsLayout="grid2"
  nav={[{ href: '#benefits', label: 'What you get' }, { href: '#faq', label: 'FAQ' }]}
  hero={{
    titleHtml: 'Welcome, Codeable experts!',
    lead: `GBTI is a professional publishing network for developers. Read the work published across it and join the conversation. Your Codeable invite covers a full year at the ${TIER_LABEL} tier, no card required.`,
    ctaLabel: 'Claim your free year',
    secondaryCta: { href: '#benefits', label: 'What you get' },
    // Facts about the OFFER, not benefit claims about the tier.
    ticks: ['No card required', 'Nothing bills automatically'],
  }}
  claimStyle="classic"
  faqs={faqs}
/>
